 "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16159, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01UMvQPvj7GZc8UqF6TGyXrv", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19587, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Ta14ELSDhMTiN7HKufr74c", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks on v2.3.1 - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). Actions taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release marked healthy in production (v2.3.0 was healthy; v2.3.1 is unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial_failure, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback, which completed: all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. No new deploys were made. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure during rollback; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until fixed and validated.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025-incident-1"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 50187, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Ta14ELSDhMTiN7HKufr74c", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025-incident-1", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 50187, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Ta14ELSDhMTiN7HKufr74c", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 52388, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01USnGH5CzFmoiGG8DxC29fS", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52688, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01USnGH5CzFmoiGG8DxC29fS", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52688, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01USnGH5CzFmoiGG8DxC29fS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 55077, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions. It is healthy again, with error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release marked healthy in production. v2.3.1 was the unhealthy one, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed. I retried the same rollback once and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open for checkout-api. The first attempt to create it timed out, but it had been recorded, so I did not open a duplicate. The incident describes the rollback, the partial failure, and the retry.\n\nFollow-up for the team: investigate why v2.3.1 failed health checks and why the orchestrator halted the rollback partway. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed and validated.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Btreox45irskASgP5QDL8K", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018tHVryNEvJjt8v5JzEVcwZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release marked healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy one currently running in all three regions. Rolling back to v2.3.0, which has been healthy in production, so no change-manager approval is needed.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015eXe3YVr3BimikJaffsQFp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback reported a partial failure after us-east. I'll check the current state before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01F7p3nw32i8kPGfkBMNJoJQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout stopped after us-east. us-east is now on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. The user asked for all regions, so I'll retry the same rollback once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017yQxsnwgLQZ5Hfsw2ifNBX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UMvQPvj7GZc8UqF6TGyXrv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback completed and checkout-api is healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions. Now I'll open the SEV2 incident and record what happened, including the partial failure.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Ta14ELSDhMTiN7HKufr74c", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks on v2.3.1 - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). Actions taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release marked healthy in production (v2.3.0 was healthy; v2.3.1 is unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial_failure, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback, which completed: all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. No new deploys were made. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure during rollback; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until fixed and validated.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025-incident-1"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so I'll check whether it was created before retrying, to avoid a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01USnGH5CzFmoiGG8DxC29fS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions. It is healthy again, with error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release marked healthy in production. v2.3.1 was the unhealthy one, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed. I retried the same rollback once and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open for checkout-api. The first attempt to create it timed out, but it had been recorded, so I did not open a duplicate. The incident describes the rollback, the partial failure, and the retry.\n\nFollow-up for the team: investigate why v2.3.1 failed health checks and why the orchestrator halted the rollback partway. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed and validated.", "type": "text"}]}]}